				"_note": "bsa-study-progress-guard: a BsaWarning is the formal, signed early-warning evidence record (improvementPeriod, offeredGuidance, personalCircumstancesNote, signature) required before a negative BSA decision can survive appeal — an append-only signed-evidence archetype, mirroring Attestation. Body leads with the warning fields (8-wide) and a Related panel resolving learner, programme and the originating flag. No comms leaves (no linkedTypes) — the x-openregister-notifications dialect handles the learner-facing notification on issue. Sidebar keeps metadata + audit-trail — the tamper-evidence trail is the whole point of a signed warning.",
